      },
      {
        "id": "22",
        "kind": "map",
        "params": {
          "curve": "exponential",
          "in_max": 1.0,
          "in_min": -1.0,
          "out_max": 7000.0,
          "out_min": 2000.0
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            1120.0,
            1000.0
          ],
          "label": "Brightness"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "c3",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "A Chaos attractor wanders the lowpass between 2 and 7 kHz, so some notes ring bright and some dull, never quite repeating."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            1400.0,
            1000.0
          ],
          "size": [
            420.0,
            80.0
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "17",
        "kind": "convolution",
        "config": {
          "file": "assets/hall-ir.wav",
          "channels": 2,
          "partition": 1024
        },
        "params": {
          "gain": -6.0
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            1960.0,
            300.0
          ],
          "label": "Hall"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "18",
        "kind": "mix",
        "config": {
          "inputs": 2
        },
        "params": {
          "gain_0": -2.0,
          "gain_1": 0.0
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            2240.0,
            300.0
          ],
          "label": "Dry and hall"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "19",
        "kind": "spectrogram",
        "params": {
          "window": 6.0
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            2520.0,
            300.0
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "20",
        "kind": "audio_out",
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            2880.0,
            300.0
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "c4",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "The string plays in a hall through Convolution: its impulse response (assets/hall-ir.wav) is the Hall Reverb block's echo of one click, rendered with audioc. Its partition is 1024 samples, a quarter of the CPU of the default 256 for this two-second response; the Convolution reports that as latency (21 ms), so the dry string is delayed to match before the Mix. The Spectrogram shows each note's harmonics fading, the high ones first.\n\nTry: Sustain at −0.03 dB for strings that ring for seconds; the Feedback's delay back to block to hear it go out of tune; a Formant after the Mix with an LFO on its vowel."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            1960.0,
            560.0
          ],
          "size": [
            640.0,
            176.0
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
